Skip pod preparation for warm enter and cp

Reuse the daemon's prepared pod connection so repeated enter and cp
commands avoid backend inspection, configuration loading, and setup
RPCs. Share Claude's readiness and pod identity checks while preserving
the running pod's workspace and native interactive exec transport.

Bound cached connection validation before commands or transfers begin,
so stopped pods and broken routes can fall back to preparation without
replaying commands or uploads. Keep transfer duration unrestricted.
Cover warm reuse, workspace and stdin behavior, lifecycle recovery, and
failed or stalled readiness checks with integration tests.
